      "artist": "Eric Jones",
      "description": "The central chamber of the Barclodiad-y-Gawres tomb Excavations by Powell and Daniel in 1956 showed that a cremation fire had been lit in the central chamber. This fire had been extinguished once the flesh had been burnt with a soup made of fishes, frogs and field mammals. The site then had been \"carefully covered with limpet shells, so that all the bones survived\" (Frances Lynch Gwynedd HMSO 1995 pp12)",
